      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think it is necessary to review the polygon count limit in mobile versions such as Quest.\n\nIn fact, even if it reaches 70,000 polygons, the uncompressed size will not increase much, and I think that in the mobile version, the performance rank should be Medium until it reaches 40,000 polygons.\n\nIn fact, if you try to limit the number of polygons to 15,000, which is within the default display limit of Medium in the mobile version, the appearance will be greatly disrupted.\n\nEven with 20,000 polygons that fit into Poor, the appearance will collapse depending on the combination of costume and avatar.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
