      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I generally agree with this opinion.\n\nI'll leave the middle number up to the developers, but I think the Very Poor line could be raised to around 100,000.\n\nI also think now is the time to reinstate the polygon upload limit so that users don't take that limit for granted.\n\nHowever, I think the number should be increased to 500,000, or even a more lenient 1 million.\n\nJust like the TextMemory limit is 500MB.\n\n(Personally, I think a limit of around 300,000 would be fine, but I think there are many players who don't agree, so we need to be careful.)\n\nIn many cases, people who can't even manage the most understandable number, the number of polygons, often end up with equally poor textures and PhysBones.\n\nRather than limiting the polygons themselves, we should reinstate the limit, saying, \"If you can't even manage easy-to-understand numbers, you don't deserve to upload.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
